# Keep the byte-hashed machine schema identical across platforms and clones.
Reproducibility?Packet/schema/schema.json text eol=lf

# Same reason, for every other file whose RAW BYTES are hashed by a pin somewhere
# in the project. This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true,
# so an unpinned text file materializes as CRLF in a fresh clone and any raw-byte
# digest taken from it breaks. Verified 2026-07-29: draft-config-v0.1.json is
# already CRLF in the development working tree while the assignment JSON beside it
# is LF, so the divergence is real rather than hypothetical.
#
# Note that pinning is defence in depth only. Code that hashes these files folds
# CRLF to LF in memory before digesting, so the pins below are not what makes a
# digest portable -- they make the raw bytes agree with the canonical bytes too.
Reproducibility?Packet/config/proposed-gate3-assignment-v0.1.json text eol=lf
Reproducibility?Packet/protocol/*.md text eol=lf
